course: dictionary
lesson: 9306
title: Spotting the meaning of speck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A speck is a very small spot, mark or piece of something. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «One speck of dust can ruin a chip» tells you that a speck is tiny, because one small piece is enough to cause a problem.
explain: Speck can also mean something so far away that it looks like a tiny dot. «The plane was just a speck in the sky.» A plane is big, but from the ground it looks very small. Test your meaning by swapping in a tiny dot, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look out for the phrase «a speck of» and the phrase «not a speck». «There was not a speck of dust on the shelf» means there was no dust at all. The words «not a» are the clue that the answer is nothing.
fact: A speck is a very small spot, mark or piece of something.
fact: «A speck of dust» means one tiny piece of dust.
fact: Speck can also mean something far away that looks like a tiny dot, such as «a speck in the sky».
fact: «Not a speck» is a phrase that means none at all.
fact: Specks of dust, pollen and skin flakes float in the air, and you can see them in a sunbeam.
exercise: «Air is full of tiny specks of dust, pollen and skin flakes.» What is a speck? | A loud noise in the room | A very large piece of rock | A kind of bird that sings | *A very small spot or piece of something
exercise: «The plane was just a speck in the sky.» What does speck mean here? | A large, bright cloud | A shadow on the ground | A loud engine noise | *Something so far away it looks like a tiny dot
exercise: In «Air is full of tiny specks of dust», which word tells you the specks are small? | *tiny | Full | dust | Air
test: «One speck of dust can ruin a chip.» What does this sentence tell you about specks? | Dust is good for computers | Chips are always made in dirty rooms | Specks are always big and heavy | *Even a tiny speck can cause a lot of harm
test: «There was not a speck of dust on the shelf.» What does not a speck mean? | There was some dust in the corner | There was dust on the floor only | There was a lot of dust on the shelf | *There was no dust at all
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to speck in «a speck of dirt on the window»? | Shout | *Spot | Window | Mountain
